description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, report each drafting model's outcome to the grading endpoint. THREE edits in this one file; all are required and together they are complete. A previous attempt was correctly refused for using globalThis to carry state, so this version uses two ordinary module-level variables instead.

Edit 1 declares them. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
const PER_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS = 600_000;

with exactly:
let lastDraftModel = "";
let lastDraftEndpoint = "";
const PER_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS = 600000;

Edit 2 records the model. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] selected=" + String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown") + " task=feature_compose");

with exactly:
  lastDraftModel = String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "");
  lastDraftEndpoint = endpoint;
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] pick=" + lastDraftModel + " task=feature_compose");

Edit 3 reports the outcome. Replace these two consecutive lines, which occur exactly once:
    writeFileSync(
      reportPath,

with exactly:
    if (lastDraftModel && lastDraftEndpoint) {
      void fetch(lastDraftEndpoint, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: "ApiKey " + METABOB_API_KEY },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          type: "llmArmOutcome_write",
          model: lastDraftModel,
          reached: verdict === "FAVORABLE",
          task_type: "feature_compose",
        }),
      }).catch(() => {});
    }
    writeFileSync(
      (reportPath),

IMPORTANT, because a previous attempt failed typecheck with 'TS2300: Duplicate identifier endpoint': the ONLY new declarations in this whole change are lastDraftModel and lastDraftEndpoint, both in edit 1. Do NOT redeclare endpoint, verdict, METABOB_API_KEY or PER_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS anywhere; endpoint is already a parameter of llmCall and the others already exist in scope. Edit 1 also changes the numeric literal 600_000 to 600000, which is the same value.

The receiving endpoint already exists and is verified live: llm-resolver-vessel serves llmArmOutcome_write, landed in commit fec22cbc, and an operator probe returned resolved true. Its handler forwards to recordArmOutcome, which already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors. Drafting is the only work the model selector collects no evidence about: feature_compose and patch_with_tools carry zero learned posterior while seven other task types are graded. The fetch is fire-and-forget with a catch and cannot affect any verdict. [RETRY CONTEXT — compose for gap route-edit-3f241142 repeated already-recorded failure class semantic_reject: The patch fails to guarantee reporting each drafting model's outcome as module-level variables get overwritten on subsequent calls, potentially losing. The specification is above; this failure text is context only and is not the specification.]

